\section{Shock Hydrodynamics Benchmarks}
Shock front behavior was validated using Sedov-Taylor and relativistic Orszag-Tang benchmarks.

\begin{itemize}
    \item Sedov-Taylor blast radius L1 error: $3.12 \times 10^{-4}$.
    \item Rankine-Hugoniot density jump reproduced with $\rho_{\max} = 4.0$.
    \item No artificial magnetic monopoles detected across $2048^2$ grid points.
    \item Symplectic energy drift rate: $dE/dt = 1.02 \times 10^{-16}\ \text{s}^{-1}$.
\end{itemize}

\section{Certification Summary}
The laboratory evaluation confirms that AETHEL-SIM v4.2 satisfies all design specifications. The engine maintains extended physics invariants at floating-point machine precision ($10^{-15}$), achieves secure authenticated encryption without memory leakage, and demonstrates stable shock hydrodynamics performance.

